      <div class="article__main">
        <div class="article__body prose">
          <blockquote>
<ul>
<li><strong>Quick answer:</strong> GTA 6 needs <strong>up to 212 GB</strong>. PlayStation says to keep <strong>at least 212 GB free</strong> on PS5.</li>
<li><strong>Pre-load (downloading the game early) opened on 10 Nov 2026.</strong> Boxed copies have a <strong>download code, not a disc</strong>, and reached shops on <strong>12 Nov</strong>.</li>
<li><strong>It stays locked until midnight in your time zone on 19 Nov.</strong> Pre-loading does not let you play early. See the <a href="release-time.md">release time table</a>.</li>
</ul>
</blockquote>
<p><strong>Words used on this page.</strong> <em>GB</em> means gigabytes, the size of a file. <em>Storage</em> is the space on your console. <em>Rest Mode</em> (PS5) and <em>Sleep mode</em> (Xbox) keep the console on at low power so it can download.</p>
<h2 id="step-1-check-how-much-space-you-have" tabindex="-1">Step 1: Check how much space you have</h2>
<p><strong>PS5</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Go to the home screen.</li>
<li>Open <strong>Settings</strong>.</li>
<li>Select <strong>Storage</strong>.</li>
<li>Read the free space. You need <strong>more than 212 GB</strong>. Take extra for patches.</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Xbox Series X|S</strong> <em>(general Xbox menu path, check the names on your console)</em></p>
<ol>
<li>Press the <strong>Xbox button</strong> on your controller.</li>
<li>Go to <strong>Profile &amp; system</strong>, then <strong>Settings</strong>.</li>
<li>Select <strong>System</strong>, then <strong>Storage devices</strong>.</li>
<li>Read the free space. You need <strong>more than 212 GB</strong>.</li>
</ol>
<p>![PS5 Storage screen showing free space](TODO: image:preload-size-step-1 — menu screen, PS5: Settings &gt; Storage with the free-space bar visible)
<em>Caption: Menu screen. The PS5 storage screen showing free space.</em></p>
<p>![Xbox storage devices screen showing free space](TODO: image:preload-size-step-2 — menu screen, Xbox: Settings &gt; System &gt; Storage devices with free space visible)
<em>Caption: Menu screen. The Xbox storage screen showing free space.</em></p>
<h2 id="step-2-make-room-if-you-are-short" tabindex="-1">Step 2: Make room if you are short</h2>
<ol>
<li>Pick one old game you do not play.</li>
<li>Delete it, or move it to another storage device.</li>
<li>Check your free space again.</li>
<li>Repeat until you have <strong>more than 212 GB</strong> free.</li>
</ol>
<p>PlayStation’s own advice is to delete data or move it to a different storage device.</p>
<h2 id="step-3-start-the-download" tabindex="-1">Step 3: Start the download</h2>
<p><strong>PS5</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Open <strong>Game Library</strong>.</li>
<li>Select <strong>Grand Theft Auto VI</strong>.</li>
<li>Select <strong>Download</strong>.</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Xbox Series X|S</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Press the <strong>Xbox button</strong>.</li>
<li>Open <strong>My games &amp; apps</strong>.</li>
<li>Select <strong>Full library</strong>.</li>
<li>Select <strong>Grand Theft Auto VI</strong>, then <strong>Install</strong>.</li>
</ol>
<p>Bought the boxed version? There is a code inside, not a disc. Enter it first:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>PS5:</strong> sign in, select your avatar at the top of the screen, select <strong>Redeem Code</strong>, then enter the code.</li>
<li><strong>Xbox:</strong> redeem the code in the Microsoft Store (menu names on your console may differ).</li>
</ul>
<p>![PS5 GTA VI game page with the Download button](TODO: image:preload-size-step-3 — step screenshot, PS5: GTA VI page with the Download button highlighted)
<em>Caption: Step screenshot. Select Download on the PS5 game page.</em></p>
<h2 id="step-4-let-it-finish-while-you-sleep" tabindex="-1">Step 4: Let it finish while you sleep</h2>
<p><strong>PS5</strong> (official PlayStation steps)</p>
<ol>
<li>Open <strong>Settings &gt; Saved Data and Game/App Settings &gt; Automatic Updates</strong>.</li>
<li>Turn on <strong>Auto-Install in Rest Mode</strong>.</li>
<li>Open <strong>Settings &gt; System &gt; Power Saving &gt; Features Available in Rest Mode</strong>.</li>
<li>Turn on <strong>Stay Connected to the Internet</strong>.</li>
<li>Open the Control Center, select <strong>Power</strong>, then <strong>Enter Rest Mode</strong>.</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Xbox Series X|S</strong> <em>(general Xbox menu path, check on your console)</em></p>
<ol>
<li>Press the <strong>Xbox button</strong>, then open <strong>Profile &amp; system &gt; Settings</strong>.</li>
<li>Go to <strong>System &gt; Updates</strong> and turn on the options to keep your console and your games up to date.</li>
<li>Keep the console <strong>on or in Sleep mode</strong>, not fully off, so the download can continue.</li>
</ol>
<p>![PS5 Rest Mode settings screen with both options on](TODO: image:preload-size-step-4 — menu screen, PS5: Features Available in Rest Mode with Stay Connected to the Internet on)
<em>Caption: Menu screen. PS5 Rest Mode settings that let the download continue.</em></p>
<h2 id="the-numbers" tabindex="-1">The numbers</h2>
<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="table">
<thead>
<tr>
