</tr>
<tr>
<td>100 Mbps</td>
<td>4.5 hours</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>4G fixed wireless</td>
<td>More than 10 hours</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></div>
<p>Use a cable (Ethernet) if you can. It is more stable than Wi-Fi.</p>
<h2 id="download-stuck-fix-it-in-this-order" tabindex="-1">Download stuck? Fix it in this order</h2>
<p><strong>PS5</strong> (official PlayStation steps)</p>
<ol>
<li>Open <strong>Downloads/Uploads</strong> in the Control Center.</li>
<li>Select the GTA VI download.</li>
<li>Select <strong>Pause</strong>, then select <strong>Resume</strong>.</li>
<li>Still stuck? Select the download and choose <strong>Cancel and Delete</strong>.</li>
<li>Go back to <strong>Game Library</strong> and select <strong>Download</strong> again.</li>
<li>Still stuck? Check four things: you are on the account that bought the game, the console is online, you have enough space, and your system software is up to date.</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Xbox Series X|S</strong> <em>(general Xbox steps, check on your console)</em></p>
<ol>
<li>Press the <strong>Xbox button</strong> and open <strong>My games &amp; apps</strong>.</li>
<li>Open the <strong>Queue</strong> and highlight GTA VI.</li>
<li>Press the <strong>Menu button</strong> (the three-lines button) and pause, then resume.</li>
<li>Still stuck? Cancel it and install again from <strong>Full library</strong>.</li>
<li>Check account, internet and space, as above.</li>
</ol>
<p>Who to ask: PlayStation Support or Xbox Support for downloads and codes. Rockstar Support for gameplay problems, patches and bugs.</p>
<h2 id="patches-reported-not-official" tabindex="-1">Patches (reported, not official)</h2>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Rumour / unconfirmed:</strong> Vice reports that dataminers (people who read game files) found a patch around 13 Nov (about 1 GB) and another from 16 Nov (about 602.5 MB on PS5, 1.6 GB on Xbox), rolling out slowly. Rockstar had published <strong>no patch notes</strong> as of 16 Nov. Source: <a href="https://www.vice.com/en/article/gta-6-second-day-one-patch-ps5-xbox/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">https://www.vice.com/en/article/gta-6-second-day-one-patch-ps5-xbox/</a></p>
</blockquote>
<p>The final launch-day update size is <strong>not announced</strong>.</p>
<h2 id="faq" tabindex="-1">FAQ</h2>
<h3 id="how-big-is-the-gta-6-download" tabindex="-1">How big is the GTA 6 download?</h3>
<p>Up to 212 GB. PlayStation says keep at least 212 GB free on PS5.</p>
<h3 id="when-did-gta-6-pre-load-start" tabindex="-1">When did GTA 6 pre-load start?</h3>
<p>10 November 2026. PS5 at midnight local time. Xbox at midnight GMT.</p>
<h3 id="can-i-pre-load-the-boxed-version" tabindex="-1">Can I pre-load the boxed version?</h3>
<p>Yes. Enter the code from the box on your console store. There is no disc.</p>
<h3 id="can-i-play-early-if-the-pre-load-is-done" tabindex="-1">Can I play early if the pre-load is done?</h3>
<p>No. The game unlocks at midnight in your time zone on 19 November.</p>
<h3 id="my-download-will-not-start-what-now" tabindex="-1">My download will not start. What now?</h3>
<p>Pause and resume. Then cancel and download again. Then check account, internet, space and updates.</p>
